			<p>
						<table width="95%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" class="border" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#447">Guild Philosophy</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							I was asked to re-post this so here it is in all it's GLORY. I will add/delete things as my opinion changes over time when I learn things about guilds and their management. This will be a living document reflecting my attitude and hopefully everone elses attitudes toward what is important in a guild. It is, hopefully, what everyone wants out of one.<br />
<br />
Hello everyone!<br />
Who am I?? I am the Jack of all trades and master of none. I am the one insulting Zyleena, Crystleyes and a few others as eight (Yes EIGHT!) different characters on Rodcet Nife server. <br />
<br />
I want to welcome all the new members to “Elite Mystic Force” (EMF) and say “Hi!” formally, to all the old ones. Even the ones I don’t see anymore (Beal and Tarnon since they have outgrown (hehehe) most of us). And Yes, there are a lot of little people (Lvls 5-25) running around out there with our Guild Tag on despite our lvl limit. I think this is good and promotes camaraderie and the sense of a “Family”.  <br />
<br />
I know I enjoy playing my low levels a lot since we (guildees) can group together with most others in EMF. You can always see “Good times” flying across the guild chat channel and I apologize to those that get spammed when they are trying to communicate in a group that is not of EMF. I know I have had problems with other guilds at times because of the spam of people just “Talking” about non-game related stuff. <br />
Yes Gen, I know most are ALTs to higher lvl members, and personally I never felt a level limit was needed in a guild if there were representatives of the guild across all the levels (Hey, there’s an Idea for Officer Status… Officers of the guild are restricted to Lvl ranges and once they move out of that level range they go back into the Pot if there are already Officer slots filled in those levels if we need officers for that purpose)<br />
<br />
I guess I wanted to post something on my philosophies of what a guild is, and what the guild FOCUS should be. <br />
<br />
To me, a guild isn’t a bunch of  “UBER” players twinked to the hilt and solely out to “Farm” an area for cash and super items. Don’t get me wrong, I “LIKE” UBER items and am extremely happy to get them for my characters. BUT!…I am not playing this game to get 1,000,000,000 Plat in the bank or have the BEST equipment money can buy. <br />
With my personal schedule (Wife and twins) I cannot go “RAID” a place every day like other UBER guilds (Eastern Keep, Dragons Fist, Inner Stronghold,  Casters Alliance, Noble Alliance to name a few) to get Great drops and grind everyone for exp on a preset schedule. My lifestyle (nor does my Wife) doesn’t permit this. I hope the members we have in the guild are of like philosophies because from what I have learned, EMF’s leadership (At this time) doesn’t have the time to plan raids of this caliber and we don’t have our “Long range plan” set to have everyone get there Epics and have (10+), LVL 60’s by the end of the year. <br />
It’s Just not gonna happen with this set of people. Hehehehe. If you are looking for that type of guild, then you are in the wrong family. I am personally sorry as I like everyone I have met so far. Achieving that level and item is a great goal for a character and player, but this is the wrong guild for it. We may get to epics later, as we are getting good solid characters in the guild and people are moving up rapidly. But we aren’t “Epic/Dragon Raid” hunting as of yet. <br />
<br />
What I have included below was written to me in an E-mail from one of the new members that migrated over from Eci server. I will admit to recruiting my personal friends that were part of our regular group on Eci server (which is why I wanted EMF to be started there) and glad they finally chose to start characters here. They are loosing a lot playing on Rodcet, but also (I feel) gaining a lot since we have fun in EMF. <br />
<br />
<br />
1. A guild should provide greater opportunity to get in groups. So all members of a guild should feel confident that when they log on, they have others to group without having to waste time seeking a group. Obviously, guild size and level distribution are limiting factors to this, which is why guild leadership must take great pains to insure that this aspect can or will be met.<br />
<br />
2. Guilds must constantly grow, so guild leaders must recruit new players actively, but pre-determine how fast that growth should occur. Additionally, when a new member is allowed to join, leadership should make every effort (“Try” is a better word since numbers of members and level distribution will affect this ability) to place that person in group, even trying different things until it is clear that the member has a regular game experience. <br />
<br />
3. Only a Guild can accomplish certain quests or raids to full potential, (this is) because of the ability to communicate, and (their) familiarity with each other (and each persons character abilities). <br />
<br />
They (Guilds) are about good people getting together to have fun and group. But always there is a danger in these things for a guild to overlook Item (1) above because of the pursuit of (2). The question is how can you do both. If a guild chooses only one of the two items, for me it has to be Item (1). Because that’s the more important one. <br />
And (3) everyone wants, and we are finally getting the levels needed to do this in EMF. It just won’t be a regular thing since we all have a REAL life and time is precious. I agree with the three points of a guild above and will do my best to support people in the guild when I can (keyword “WHEN”). <br />
<br />
Welcome all, don’t die in game, and Have a GREAT time.
						</td>
